{"prompt": "Explain how a refrigerator transfers heat in one detailed paragraph.", "prompt_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 814, 20139, 1204, 264, 43447, 29612, 8364, 303, 799, 11346, 13901, 13, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "tokens": [32, 43447, 29612, 8364, 539, 68213, 279, 28868, 57880, 5706, 314, 264, 51926, 28417, 505, 421, 35456, 287, 9956, 4203, 1881, 14058, 321, 6605, 5134, 11, 13057, 6992, 27462, 4649, 494, 279, 8981, 14362, 310, 279, 43442, 26383, 4424, 2272, 279, 5629, 19556, 314, 8364, 6195, 13, 561, 1817, 11690, 303, 279, 57054, 824, 68366, 7172, 4613, 279, 36337, 11, 1332, 264, 3238, 85416, 14058, 28417, 505, 86914, 8364, 494, 279, 3487, 321, 3594, 11, 13969, 424, 310, 57054, 344, 1083, 264, 6605, 26, 411, 41702, 314, 40290, 8364, 1027, 2971, 279, 14362, 13, 561, 338, 507, 757, 28417, 505, 369, 1179, 14336, 1083, 264, 56885, 11, 864, 94616, 23835, 287, 279, 6605, 11, 11602, 7459, 1141, 7035, 321, 9039, 1472, 961, 205694, 749, 944, 13, 1061, 1496, 85416, 11, 1496, 12, 33413, 6605, 26565, 310, 279, 9464, 57438, 68366, 11, 10813, 7172, 383, 279, 1142, 466, 5445, 314, 279, 4821, 11, 1332, 424, 18652, 279, 38734, 8364, 310, 279, 14170, 2956, 3594, 11, 13969, 279, 28417, 505, 310, 9464, 1081, 1142, 1083, 264, 14058, 13, 16864, 11, 279, 14058, 28417, 505, 15734, 1472, 449, 14046, 30396, 466, 1994, 33360, 13311, 11], "text": "A refrigerator transfers heat by exploiting the thermodynamic properties of a circulating refrigerant that undergoes phase changes between liquid and gas states, effectively moving thermal energy from the cold interior to the warmer exterior environment against the natural gradient of heat flow. The process begins in the evaporator coils located inside the fridge, where a low-pressure liquid refrigerant absorbs heat from the food and air, causing it to evaporate into a gas; this absorption of latent heat cools the interior. The gaseous refrigerant is then drawn into a compressor, which mechanically compresses the gas, significantly increasing its pressure and temperature through adiabatic work. This high-pressure, high-temperature gas flows to the condenser coils, typically located on the back or bottom of the unit, where it releases the accumulated heat to the surrounding room air, causing the refrigerant to condense back into a liquid. Finally, the liquid refrigerant passes through an expansion valve or capillary tube,", "done": "DONE 192 24 465.7 4385.8 length 107 178 0", "request_wall_seconds": 4.848249481001403, "resources_before": {"memory_events": {"low": 0, "high": 0, "max": 0, "oom": 0, "oom_kill": 0, "oom_group_kill": 0, "sock_throttled": 0}, "memory_current": 38385971200, "cpu_stat": {"usage_usec": 3363301215, "user_usec": 3291830879, "system_usec": 71470335, "nice_usec": 0, "core_sched.force_idle_usec": 0, "nr_periods": 0, "nr_throttled": 0, "throttled_usec": 0, "nr_bursts": 0, "burst_usec": 0}, "memory_pressure": "some avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=89150\nfull avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=89150", "guest_cpu_ticks": [7708630, 666, 488218, 134645687, 639957, 0, 68666, 4808, 48398, 0], "process_io": {"rchar": 37878947620, "wchar": 9932, "syscr": 20672, "syscw": 970, "read_bytes": 38721007616, "write_bytes": 12288, "cancelled_write_bytes": 0}, "io_pressure": "some avg10=0.91 avg60=9.36 avg300=10.83 total=1103391812\nfull avg10=0.88 avg60=8.92 avg300=10.40 total=1050584730", "smaps_rollup": {"Rss": 35597776, "Pss_Anon": 35093332, "AnonHugePages": 0}, "process_minor_faults": 9070162, "process_major_faults": 1, "process_cpu_ticks": 31857}, "resources_after": {"memory_events": {"low": 0, "high": 0, "max": 0, "oom": 0, "oom_kill": 0, "oom_group_kill": 0, "sock_throttled": 0}, "memory_current": 38386061312, "cpu_stat": {"usage_usec": 3401536720, "user_usec": 3329965764, "system_usec": 71570955, "nice_usec": 0, "core_sched.force_idle_usec": 0, "nr_periods": 0, "nr_throttled": 0, "throttled_usec": 0, "nr_bursts": 0, "burst_usec": 0}, "memory_pressure": "so