{"prompt": "Explain how a suspension bridge carries its loads in one detailed paragraph.", "prompt_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 814, 20139, 1204, 264, 23538, 13759, 22651, 1141, 20269, 303, 799, 11346, 13901, 13, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "tokens": [32, 23538, 13759, 22651, 1141, 20269, 1472, 264, 25924, 1785, 314, 22770, 5792, 5176, 7731, 11, 1332, 279, 5839, 23016, 5255, 944, 303, 20196, 310, 8059, 4528, 494, 279, 9249, 310, 279, 4751, 13, 561, 1817, 11690, 440, 279, 11795, 9022, 1601, 34878, 11, 864, 14255, 494, 279, 1822, 23538, 34878, 321, 5774, 1761, 279, 13759, 9249, 11, 48270, 279, 3756, 321, 5418, 20269, 38453, 310, 279, 1822, 34878, 13, 4081, 1822, 34878, 11, 86788, 888, 279, 31352, 314, 279, 38409, 11, 513, 35798, 310, 36534, 21330, 448, 8177, 26, 430, 781, 28741, 1172, 279, 4528, 314, 279, 9249, 11, 781, 6707, 15725, 28908, 82, 421, 4336, 2272, 279, 38409, 11, 864, 303, 2404, 28323, 1439, 11795, 20269, 1441, 310, 836, 39144, 13, 4319, 484, 19698, 11, 279, 15725, 3566, 314, 279, 22770, 303, 279, 1822, 34878, 369, 64077, 539, 10632, 16602, 1098, 506, 2892, 809, 314, 279, 13759, 11, 864, 33170, 279, 6601, 321, 5190, 279, 34878, 494, 7435, 5830, 680, 11, 26600, 19720, 279, 5689, 7993, 44589, 5893, 13, 1061, 53454, 24546, 421, 279, 4307, 5759, 8198, 14733, 11, 440, 279, 38409, 11256, 24315, 321, 279, 34878, 11256, 22770, 11], "text": "A suspension bridge carries its loads through a sophisticated system of tension-based force distribution, where the primary structural elements work in concert to transfer weight from the deck to the ground. The process begins with the vertical suspender cables, which hang from the main suspension cables and directly support the bridge deck, transferring the live and dead loads upward to the main cables. These main cables, draped over the tops of the towers, are subjected to immense tensile forces; as they sag under the weight of the deck, they generate horizontal thrusts that push against the towers, which in turn transmit these vertical loads down to their foundations. Simultaneously, the horizontal component of the tension in the main cables is resisted by massive anchorages at either end of the bridge, which absorb the pull and prevent the cables from straightening out, thereby maintaining the necessary catenary shape. This equilibrium ensures that the entire structure remains stable, with the towers handling compression and the cables handling tension,", "done": "DONE 192 26 449.5 4444.8 length 97 160 0", "request_wall_seconds": 4.890685626975028, "resources_before": {"memory_events": {"low": 0, "high": 0, "max": 0, "oom": 0, "oom_kill": 0, "oom_group_kill": 0, "sock_throttled": 0}, "memory_current": 38386020352, "cpu_stat": {"usage_usec": 3401733533, "user_usec": 3330095648, "system_usec": 71637885, "nice_usec": 0, "core_sched.force_idle_usec": 0, "nr_periods": 0, "nr_throttled": 0, "throttled_usec": 0, "nr_bursts": 0, "burst_usec": 0}, "memory_pressure": "some avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=89150\nfull avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=89150", "guest_cpu_ticks": [7712513, 666, 488241, 134645771, 639957, 0, 68667, 4808, 48399, 0], "process_io": {"rchar": 37878947790, "wchar": 11485, "syscr": 20673, "syscw": 1169, "read_bytes": 38721007616, "write_bytes": 12288, "cancelled_write_bytes": 0}, "io_pressure": "some avg10=0.50 avg60=8.47 avg300=10.61 total=1103392542\nfull avg10=0.48 avg60=8.07 avg300=10.19 total=1050584730", "smaps_rollup": {"Rss": 35597788, "Pss_Anon": 35093344, "AnonHugePages": 0}, "process_minor_faults": 9098894, "process_major_faults": 1, "process_cpu_ticks": 35685}, "resources_after": {"memory_events": {"low": 0, "high": 0, "max": 0, "oom": 0, "oom_kill": 0, "oom_group_kill": 0, "sock_throttled": 0}, "memory_current": 38386081792, "cpu_stat": {"usage_usec": 3440210310, "user_usec": 3368469496, "system_usec": 71740814, "nice_usec": 0, "core_sched.force_idle_usec": 0, "nr_periods": 0, "nr_throttled": 0, "throttled_usec": 0, 