{"prompt": "Explain how fiber-optic communication transmits information in one detailed paragraph.", "prompt_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 814, 20139, 1204, 23043, 54227, 291, 10222, 1308, 43220, 1928, 303, 799, 11346, 13901, 13, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "tokens": [37, 8365, 54227, 291, 10222, 1308, 43220, 1928, 539, 32328, 19132, 16779, 1083, 3000, 63248, 11, 10813, 7658, 539, 264, 19861, 466, 12733, 11, 864, 513, 1179, 31511, 1472, 264, 14979, 11, 18209, 40115, 314, 8720, 466, 11840, 23043, 13, 1061, 17822, 32530, 383, 279, 16988, 314, 2702, 5138, 21172, 11, 1332, 279, 3000, 369, 42837, 2785, 279, 23043, 579, 6007, 539, 264, 14170, 1145, 2903, 6000, 440, 264, 4570, 18766, 2932, 1857, 11, 21873, 421, 279, 3000, 292, 28966, 974, 279, 6007, 29618, 2903, 3622, 321, 33060, 1248, 25704, 440, 16866, 8028, 4557, 466, 90871, 13, 1577, 279, 3000, 63248, 55492, 11, 781, 6564, 795, 19873, 430, 25407, 303, 19987, 11, 9956, 11, 466, 11304, 11, 13661, 7620, 17955, 318, 11185, 8, 421, 7618, 310, 279, 3889, 1928, 13, 2332, 279, 11955, 809, 11, 264, 4355, 342, 294, 1213, 31637, 1439, 3000, 63248, 1142, 1083, 19132, 16779, 11, 864, 513, 1179, 14789, 539, 13934, 6875, 310, 42377, 279, 3889, 795, 11, 10377, 364, 1496, 65393, 2998, 11, 3238, 95013, 2179, 11, 321, 11639, 61435, 2792, 10222, 888, 12401, 25704, 13, 248046], "text": "Fiber-optic communication transmits information by converting electrical signals into light pulses, typically generated by a laser or LED, which are then guided through a thin, flexible strand of glass or plastic fiber. This transmission relies on the principle of total internal reflection, where the light is confined within the fiber's core by a surrounding cladding layer with a lower refractive index, ensuring that the light bounces off the core-cladding interface and travels long distances with minimal signal loss or attenuation. As the light pulses propagate, they carry data encoded as variations in intensity, phase, or frequency, representing binary digits (bits) that correspond to the original information. At the receiving end, a photodetector converts these light pulses back into electrical signals, which are then processed by electronic equipment to reconstruct the original data, allowing for high-bandwidth, low-latency, and noise-immune communication over vast distances.<|im_end|>", "done": "DONE 182 27 514.6 4492.3 stop 102 173 0", "request_wall_seconds": 5.003493733005598, "resources_before": {"memory_events": {"low": 0, "high": 0, "max": 0, "oom": 0, "oom_kill": 0, "oom_group_kill": 0, "sock_throttled": 0}, "memory_current": 38386036736, "cpu_stat": {"usage_usec": 3440417760, "user_usec": 3368604085, "system_usec": 71813675, "nice_usec": 0, "core_sched.force_idle_usec": 0, "nr_periods": 0, "nr_throttled": 0, "throttled_usec": 0, "nr_bursts": 0, "burst_usec": 0}, "memory_pressure": "some avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=89150\nfull avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=89150", "guest_cpu_ticks": [7716420, 666, 488265, 134645865, 639957, 0, 68668, 4808, 48399, 0], "process_io": {"rchar": 37878947972, "wchar": 13032, "syscr": 20674, "syscw": 1368, "read_bytes": 38721007616, "write_bytes": 12288, "cancelled_write_bytes": 0}, "io_pressure": "some avg10=0.33 avg60=7.93 avg300=10.47 total=1103392857\nfull avg10=0.32 avg60=7.55 avg300=10.05 total=1050584730", "smaps_rollup": {"Rss": 35597800, "Pss_Anon": 35093356, "AnonHugePages": 0}, "process_minor_faults": 9127626, "process_major_faults": 1, "process_cpu_ticks": 39539}, "resources_after": {"memory_events": {"low": 0, "high": 0, "max": 0, "oom": 0, "oom_kill": 0, "oom_group_kill": 0, "sock_throttled": 0}, "memory_current": 38386102272, "cpu_stat": {"usage_usec": 3479294997, "user_usec": 3407362707, "system_usec": 71932290, "nice_usec": 0, "core_sched.force_idle_usec": 0, "nr_periods": 0, "nr_throttled": 0, "throttled_usec": 0, "nr_bursts": 0, "burst_usec": 0}, "memory_pressure": "some avg10=0.00 avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=891